cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use qinjing in your work, please cite it as below."
title: qinjing
authors:
  - name: xycxmz
type: dataset
version: 2026.11.2
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/xycxmz/qinjing-public"
abstract: >-
  A live-executable benchmark suite for host intrusion detection (HIDS)
  capability. It ships 1076 cases (120 benign false-positive probes and
  956 attack cases mapped to MITRE ATT&CK), a runner that executes each
  case under throwaway uids with per-case session isolation, an
  alert-attribution scorer, a tight-window false-positive checker, a
  selftest gate chain, and a self-contained coverage dashboard. Any HIDS
  that can export alerts as JSON can be graded against the same corpus.
keywords:
  - hids
  - intrusion-detection
  - benchmark
  - attack-simulation
  - threat-detection
  - mitre-att&ck
  - detection-engineering
